-- Bitemporal RECALL through a SHARED thunk (smucclaw/l4-ide#914 §2B) — the
-- adversarial-review regression. A named binding containing RECALL is one
-- shared thunk; used under different temporal scopes it must answer PER
-- SCOPE (a read-only ledger force is WHNFWhen-cached on the axes it
-- observed: snapshot per scope), not serve the first scope's answer to all
-- later uses. Pre-fix this printed LIST 7, 9, 7, 7, 7, 7 — the first
-- scope's answer (vt-2023 -> 7) leaked into every later use, including the
-- AS OF 2020 read that should see an empty ledger.
--
-- Harness clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z.

IMPORT prelude

r MEANS fromMaybe 0 (RECALL `rate`)

-- expected: LIST 7, 9, 7, 9, 0, 9 — same answers as bitemporal-recall.l4's
-- inline RECALLs, but every read goes through the ONE shared binding r:
-- writes 7 (vt 2023) and 9 (vt 2024), then r under mid-2023 -> 7, r under
-- mid-2024 -> 9, r under AS OF 2020 -> 0 (everything tx-hidden), bare r -> 9.
#EVAL LIST (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2023) (RECORD `rate` IS 7)), (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2024) (RECORD `rate` IS 9)), (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2023) r), (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2024) r), (`EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) r), r
